# Fixed-width initializer overflow is rejected

Verifies an `int64[]` literal rejects an initializer that cannot be represented
at the declared width instead of widening it.

>>> source
let values: int64[] = [999999999999999999999999999999]

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `999999999999999999999999999999` for type `int64`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 23, end: 53 }

<<< exit
1
